From 393b761bedc95ffe9444a8cec3f44a5424d740b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Resti <15180778+restiyanada@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:48:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Milestone 6: order access recovery, payment proof retention,
 audit log viewer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- recover-order-access (§16.2): deviates from the PRD's phone+email pair —
  recovers by phone + order number instead, since the order number is
  already sent through every other channel (order page, all 4 emails), so
  matching it exactly is a lower bar than remembering which email was
  typed at checkout. Trade-off flagged, not hidden: order number is
  sequential per fulfilment type, not a real identity signal the way email
  is — rate limiting is the actual defense here, not the choice of fields.
  Reuses Milestone 5's accessTokenEncrypted decrypt path. Rate limited
  (§16.1/§27's 10 req/min/IP, flagged as an open gap since Milestone 1,
  never built until now) via new access_recovery_attempts table +
  lib/rate-limit.ts. lib/order-number.ts gained parseOrderNumber, the
  inverse of the existing formatOrderNumber. Frontend: /orders/find,
  linked from HomePage.
- cleanup-payment-proofs (§8/§19): 30 days after order fulfilment
  (SHIPPED/PICKED_UP), not upload time. New orders.fulfilledAt (stamped by
  scan-pickup/record-tracking) and payments.proofDeletedAt (idempotency)
  columns. Pure eligibility logic in lib/proof-retention.ts. Scheduled
  daily via pg_cron (0006 migration).
- list-audit-logs + AdminAuditLogPage (§20): not a direct RLS read as
  milestone.md originally planned — admin_users (needed for actor names)
  is deliberately not directly readable by anyone, so this follows
  list-orders' existing service-role-Edge-Function precedent instead.
  Closed a real pre-existing gap while here: audit_logs had no RLS at all.

71/71 tests pass (23 new), typecheck clean (tsc -b + deno check on every
touched/new Edge Function), oxlint clean, production build succeeds.

Not done: Web Push (Milestone 5 item 28, still open), live verification
against the real Supabase project, and a backfill plan for fulfilledAt on
orders that reached SHIPPED/PICKED_UP before this migration — see
milestone.md for details on all three.
